als all sat there and said we have  to do something we can't just sit by and  let the people suffer  so what did they do  they printed trillions of dollars and  they started throwing it everywhere they  literally were bailing out entire  industries like the airlines they were  going and sending out 1200 checks to  individuals they were manipulating  interest rates down to zero percent and  they were just handing out free money  they were extending pvp loans all over  the place and then just saying ah don't  worry you don't have to pay it back to  us  and so naturally they started a party  and they helped everybody get drunk on  free money the money was free the money  was cheap and if somebody hands you free  cheap money what do you do you start  spending it start buying things you  start investing it you start lending it  anything and everything you can do with  that money to gain any sentence of value  whether it's something for you to  consume or it's something for you to  grow the free cheap money gets put to  work and that's exactly what they wanted  they wanted to mitigate the short-term  pain they needed to drive the velocity  of money again and so they handed out  all this free cheap money now the  problem is if you do that for three  months six months nine months maybe even  12 months people don't really have time  to get used to it but if you do it for  two years  all of a sudden people start to say  themselves man i bet you they're gonna  keep giving me the free cheap money you  start to change behavior and that's  exactly what occurred we saw people  continue to act stupid and stupid and  stupid because they had free cheap money  now you can't blame them because they  had the money and the government kept  pumping more and more money into the  economy they kept interest rates  artificially low and so the party raged  on for literally 15 18 20 different  months  but back in november they realized hmm  this inflation thing that we've been  saying is transi