icially in a  recession now how the hell can we go  from a recession  to all-time high stock prices to  all-time high inflation numbers or  40-year highs and then back into a  recession all in two years well that's  because the market is manipulated all  you're watching is central banks around  the world what are they doing they  simply are jumping in the game and  they're saying every time something  happens good times we must intervene bad  times we must intervene good times we  must intervene bad times we must  intervene the volatility gets more and  more extreme  what we need in the world is free  markets we do not need people  intervening in the market let the free  market take control if they were to  allow to do that  there may be short-term pain but we  would get on a long-term record where we  would be on a path to a more sustainable  less volatile economy that's not going  to happen and so naturally we got that  1.4 annualized contraction in the  economy all of a sudden people are  waking up but it's a weird weird world  if you expect plus one percent you get  negative 1.4 percent and at the same  time all that's happening is very high  degrees of inflation at a 40-year high  what happens when the economy is  contracting and the inflation's high  well ladies and gentlemen here's what i  think is going to happen i think that  they are going to continue for the next  one or two rate hikes they're gonna keep  trying to do it they're gonna push us  further into a recession things can get  real nasty out there people are going to  panic there's going to be all sorts of  chaos and public pressure heading into  the midterm elections all of a sudden  the democratic party they're going to  tap central bankers on the shoulder apes  uncle jerome  cut it out we got to end this recession  we're going into election big dog  cut rates  get free money into the system and  probably by the end of q3 what we are  going to see is we are going to see the  federal reserve and e